<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Badia Fiorentina</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">978</span> · Also known as Badia of Florence</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Badia Fiorentina is a Benedictine abbey in the centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, founded in 978 by Willa, widow of the Margrave of Tuscany, and richly endowed by her son Hugh, whose tomb by Mino da <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fiesole">Fiesole</a> stands in the church. Its tall bell tower is a city landmark, and the abbey was closely linked with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dante-alighieri">Dante</a>'s Florence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/badia-fiorentina.jpg" alt="Badia Fiorentina" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Badia_Fiorentina_ingresso.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
